    <question>
        <text><![CDATA[An MF's Sharpe Ratio measures:]]></text>
        <answers>
            <answer correct="no"><text><![CDATA[Beta]]></text></answer>
            <answer correct="yes"><text><![CDATA[Risk-adjusted return (excess return / total risk)]]></text></answer>
            <answer correct="no"><text><![CDATA[Correlation]]></text></answer>
            <answer correct="no"><text><![CDATA[Alpha]]></text></answer>
        </answers>
        <explanation><text><![CDATA[**The Logic:** Sharpe = (Rp - Rf) / σp. Standard risk-adjusted metric.
**The Trap:** Treynor uses β; Sharpe uses σ.
**Cross-Exam Context:** Topic 20.
**Manager's Pro-Tip:** Compare Sharpe to peer group and benchmark — standalone can mislead.]]></text></explanation>
